  "_note": "Chips, rebuilt on PDTD's own scheme (config/data/chip_info). PDTD uses SEVEN quality tiers, not four, and scales a chip's number linearly with tier: a damage chip is 7% at common and 49% at ultimate (7 x tier). 'effect_per_tier' is that per-tier step, so a chip's value is always effect_per_tier x tier. Most chips are per-weapon — effect keys use the 'ow:<kind>:<stat>' form ModifierSet understands — with a handful of global ones, matching PDTD's split. merge_count is how many of one tier fuse into ONE of the next; the result is a RANDOM archetype of that higher tier (PDTD's behaviour, and what makes merging a decision rather than bookkeeping).",

